abstract: >-
  A research working draft for the Learning-Native Adaptive Software Framework
  (LNASF). It proposes a candidate component-boundary contract that makes
  observation, model updating, prediction evidence, adaptation admission,
  permitted actions, deterministic fallback, and outcome evaluation explicit.
  The candidate contribution is under validation against prior work on online
  runtime learning, ML-enabled components, self-adaptive architectures, FORMS,
  Rainbow, adaptive feedback loops, and prior usage of the learning-native
  software concept. Novelty and performance benefits are not yet established. Reference implementations demonstrate limited subsets
  only. This draft has not yet been released as a synchronized publication PDF.
